A script with top-level code (no :PROCEDURE): script-level :PARAMETERS
and :DEFAULT, top-level blocks and a trailing procedure. Top-level code
sits at column 0 and blocks indent from there (fmt.indent_style).
Suspected issue: #326 — no blank line is put between the top-level `:RETURN` and
the following `:PROCEDURE`; fmt.blank_lines_between_procs only acts after
`:ENDPROC;` / `:ENDREGION;`, but the style guide schema sets
formatting.blank_lines.before_procedure: 1 (blank_line_between_procedures).
The same gap shows in indentation/class_file between the class header and
the first method.
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nMode;
:DEFAULT nMode, 1;
:DECLARE vResult;
  :IF nMode == 1;
vResult := DoProc("LoadOne", {sSampleId});
    :ELSE;
vResult := "";
  :ENDIF;
:RETURN vResult;
:PROCEDURE LoadOne;
:PARAMETERS sId;
:RETURN sId;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nMode;
:DEFAULT nMode, 1;
:DECLARE vResult;
:IF nMode == 1;
	vResult := DoProc("LoadOne", {sSampleId});
:ELSE;
	vResult := "";
:ENDIF;
:RETURN vResult;
:PROCEDURE LoadOne;
	:PARAMETERS sId;
	:RETURN sId;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
